{number: 55}
{title: Throw Out the Life-Line}
{key: C}

{start_of_verse: 1}
[C] Throw out the Life-Line a-[F] cross the dark [C] wave,
There is a brother whom [G7] someone should [C] save;
Somebody's brother! oh, [F] who then will [C] dare
To throw out the Life-Line, his [G7] peril to [C] share?
{end_of_verse}

{start_of_chorus}
[C] Throw out the Life-Line! [F] Throw out the Life-Line!
[C] Someone is drifting a-[G7] way;
[C] Throw out the Life-Line! [F] Throw out the Life-Line!
[C] Someone is [G7] sinking to-[C] day.
{end_of_chorus}

{start_of_verse: 2}
[C] Throw out the Life-Line with [F] hand quick and [C] strong:
Why do you tarry, why [G7] linger so [C] long?
See! he is sinking; oh, [F] hasten to-[C] day,
And out with the Life-Boat! a-[G7] way, then, a-[C] way!
{end_of_verse}

{start_of_verse: 3}
[C] Throw out the Life-Line to [F] danger-fraught [C] men,
Sinking in anguish where [G7] you've never [C] been;
Winds of temptation and [F] billows of [C] woe
Will soon hurl them out where the [G7] dark waters [C] flow.
{end_of_verse}
